Source: silicon-control
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: senseikiritof <tonifede98@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms, python3
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/SenseiKiritof/Silicon-Control
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: silicon-control
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), pkexec, polkitd,
 systemd, kmod
Conflicts: ryzen-control
Replaces: ryzen-control
Recommends: stress-ng, libnotify-bin
Description: power limits, boost, undervolt and fans of the CPU, calibrated per chip
 Successor of Ryzen Control; supported so far: AMD Ryzen. Per-core Curve
 Optimizer, PPT/TDC/EDC limits, boost frequency (FMax), maximum temperature,
 power profile and motherboard fans, with modes calibrated on the CPU
 (desktops; the APUs of mini PCs and laptops: power limits), a GTK4/libadwaita
 GUI with a tray icon and a root helper (siliconctl).
 Profiles are applied at boot, with protection after a crash. Includes the
 source of the ryzen_smu kernel module, built by DKMS.
